<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Canberra, Manila boost air links.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Canberra, Manila boost air links.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia and the Philippines have agreed to expand air service capacity between the two countries by 45 percent, Australian Transport Minister John Sharp said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The expanded capacity agreed last week will accommodate the strong growth expected over the next 12 to 18 months in a market that offers great potential for the Australian tourism industry,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>About 172,000 passengers travelled between the two countries in the year to July, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
